From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:16:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: mediatek: add MT8519 power domains, ported to 6.12

The MT8519's SCPSYS power domains (ADR 0035), from MediaTek's
mt8519-pm-domains.h in Amazon's 5.4 release, wired into 6.12's shared
mtk-pm-domains.c with an mt8519-power-controller of_match entry. The data
needs three changes for 6.12's scpsys_domain_data: drop sram_ctl_offs (6.12
derives the SRAM control offset from ctl_offs), spell the bus-protection
component INFRA not INFRA_TYPE, and move the MT8519 TOP_AXI_PROT_EN register
defines into the shared include/linux/soc/mediatek/infracfg.h beside the
other SoCs'.

Builds only when a board selects the power controller; off in every current
variant.
---
 drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt8519-pm-domains.h | 186 ++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mtk-pm-domains.c    |   5 +
 include/dt-bindings/power/mt8519-power.h      |  18 ++
 include/linux/soc/mediatek/infracfg.h         |  32 +++
 4 files changed, 241 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt8519-pm-domains.h
 create mode 100644 include/dt-bindings/power/mt8519-power.h

